d 'KMEST': module to compute Kaplan-Meier survival probabilities as estimation results
d
d   kmest is intended for use in a survival time dataset set up by
d stset. It computes Kaplan-Meier survival probabilities (as
d computed by sts generate) for a list of times (sorted in
d ascending order), and/or Kaplan-Meier percentiles for a list of
d percents (srted in ascending order), and saves them as estimation
d results, without a variance matrix.  kmest is intended for use
d with the bootstrap prefix, or possibly with the jackknife prefix,
d to create confidence intervals for the Kaplan-Meier survival
d probabilities and/or percentiles, possibly allowing for
d clustering and/or sampling-probability weighting. Alternatively,
d kmest can be used with the SSC packages parmest and esetran to
d compute Greenwood confidence intervals, or delta-Greenwood
d confidence intervals using a variety of Normalizing transforms. 
d
d KW: survival data
d KW: Kaplan-Meier
d KW: probabilities
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260726
d
d Author: Roger Newson,  King's College London
d Support: email roger.newson@@kcl.ac.uk
d
f kmest.ado
f kmest_p.ado
f kmest.sthlp
